{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21720 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Naamidine H is implicated in the biological activity of CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Naamidine H acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which in turn is targeted by Cocosamide B and 7-Angeloylechinatine, and finally, all of these compounds target CCRF-HSB-2. This chain of targets indicates a potential pathway where Naamidine H may influence CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of intermediate molecules. The shared target of all these compounds at CCRF-HSB-2 suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of a common biological process, though the exact nature of this process remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction network, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the functional roles of these intermediates.",
